Subject: [RFC PATCH v1 00/18] VBS/VSM-on-KVM: QEMU support for KVM
 VM planes and the secure VM plane

This RFC adds the QEMU userspace support needed to run a Virtualization-Based
Security (VBS) / Hyper-V VSM style secure environment as an in-kernel KVM
"VM plane". It is the QEMU counterpart to the kernel series of the same name,
"[RFC PATCH VSM-ON-KVM] VBS/VSM-on-KVM: KVM VM planes and the in-kernel secure
VM plane (VTL)".

This series is the *full* QEMU VM-planes stack linearized as a clean, bisectable
history directly on mainline (v11.1.0-rc1). It folds together Joerg Roedel's
QEMU VM-planes work and the safe-tee VBS/VSM
secure-plane support. Authorship is preserved on every commit; the shortlog
below is grouped by author, and the series applies directly on upstream master
with no external base to hunt down.

The VBS/VSM portion wires up:

  - userspace handlers for the VM-plane and VBS VTL-call hypercalls that KVM
    exits to QEMU (KVM_EXIT_HYPERCALL);
  - the kvm_para.h / kvm.h header sync for the VBS VTL hypercall ABI; and
  - loading the secure-plane kernel payload and running the secure plane
    in-kernel (Option B).

Repositories (safe-tee GitHub org)
==================================

Everything needed to fetch, apply, build, and test this series is published
under the safe-tee organization on GitHub:

  - qemu:   https://github.com/safe-tee/qemu
      branch qemu-planes-v11.1.0-rc1 this series: the full QEMU VM-planes +
                                     VBS/VSM stack linearized on mainline
                                     v11.1.0-rc1 (the base-commit below).
      branch vm-planes-merged        the original merge-based integration tree
                                     this series was linearized from.

  - kernel: https://github.com/safe-tee/linux
      branch kvm-planes-v7.2-rc5     the kernel counterpart series (posted
                                     as "[RFC PATCH VSM-ON-KVM] VBS/VSM-on-
                                     KVM: KVM VM planes and the in-kernel
                                     secure VM plane (VTL)").

  - lvbs:   https://github.com/safe-tee/lvbs
      the build/test workspace, scripts, and documentation that tie the
      kernel and QEMU trees together.

Build and test
==============

The lvbs repository documents the full build-and-run flow with VM planes
enabled:

  https://github.com/safe-tee/lvbs/blob/main/docs/how-to/build.md

Quick start, from the lvbs repo root, with the linux, qemu, and lvbs trees
checked out side by side under a common workspace root:

  make kernel          # plane 0 bzImage + plane 1 vmlinux
  make secure-kernel   # standalone minimal plane-1 kernel
  make qemu            # qemu-system-x86_64
  make image           # fedora-kvm.raw (uses the secure kernel)

Acknowledgments
===============

This work stands on top of, and is indebted to, several prior efforts:

  - Joerg Roedel, whose KVM VM planes work (kernel and QEMU) this series is
    layered directly on top of, and which provides the in-kernel plane
    infrastructure that the VBS/VSM secure plane relies on.

  - Paolo Bonzini, whose "[RFC PATCH 00/29] KVM: VM planes" introduced the
    VM plane concept to KVM as a common in-kernel model for AMD VMPLs, Intel
    TDX partitions, Hyper-V VTLs, and ARM CCA planes.
    https://lwn.net/Articles/1016113/

  - James Bottomley and James Morris, for their ongoing work on VSM-on-KVM,
    which informed the design and direction of this series.

Posted as an RFC to gather feedback on the VBS-on-KVM plane model and the
VTL hypercall ABI. Comments welcome.

